{"id":"skeleton-coast-kaokoland","title":"Skeleton Coast & Kaokoland 4x4","who":"Classic 4x4 route","when":"Best May–October","vehicle":"4x4 in a convoy, 10–14 days","kind":"4x4","color":"#92400e","summary":"Namibia's wildest drive: north up the fog-bound Skeleton Coast past shipwrecks and seal colonies, inland through the desert-elephant rivers to Purros, then into Kaokoland, land of the Himba, to Epupa Falls on the Kunene and down the notorious Van Zyl's Pass into the empty Marienfluss valley. Take two vehicles, lots of fuel and water.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Skeleton Coast","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skeleton_Coast"},{"label":"Getaway: how to do the wildest 4x4 trip in Namibia","url":"https://getaway.co.za/?p=15337724"},{"label":"Wikivoyage: Kaokoland","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Kaokoland"},{"label":"Tracks4Africa: Van Zyl's Pass","url":"https://tracks4africa.co.za/listings/item/w207682/van-zyls-pass/"}],"approximate":"Usual loop from 4x4 reports; the off-road tracks are drawn as straight lines.","km":1362,"bbox":[12.47,-22.6769,14.5786,-17.0022],"stops":[{"name":"Swakopmund","place":"Swakopmund, Namibia","at":[-22.6768,14.529],"text":"Stock up in the German seaside town.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Mole%2C_Jetty_and_Lighthouse_Swakopmund%2C_Namibia.jpg/500px-Mole%2C_Jetty_and_Lighthouse_Swakopmund%2C_Namibia.jpg","page":"Swakopmund","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mole%2C_Jetty_and_Lighthouse_Swakopmund%2C_Namibia.jpg","credit":"Olga Ernst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Henties Bay","place":"Henties Bay, Namibia","at":[-22.116,14.2827],"text":"North on the salt road; the Zeila wreck south of town."},{"name":"Torra Bay","place":"Torra Bay, Namibia","at":[-20.312,13.238],"text":"Through the Ugab gate into the Skeleton Coast park."},{"name":"Terrace Bay","place":"Terrace Bay, Namibia","at":[-19.995,13.034],"text":"The northernmost point you can drive; dunes begin beyond.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Terrace_Bay_ON.JPG/500px-Terrace_Bay_ON.JPG","page":"Terrace Bay","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Terrace_Bay_ON.JPG","credit":"P199","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Sesfontein","place":"Sesfontein, Namibia","at":[-19.1232,13.6176],"text":"Inland through the Springbokwasser gate to an old fort.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Fort_Sesfontein_1.jpg/500px-Fort_Sesfontein_1.jpg","page":"Sesfontein","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_Sesfontein_1.jpg","credit":"Johan Hoffman","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Purros","place":"Purros, Namibia","at":[-18.737,12.944],"text":"Along the sandy Hoarusib riverbed, desert elephant country."},{"name":"Opuwo","place":"Opuwo, Namibia","at":[-18.055,13.8387],"text":"Kaokoland's only town: last fuel."},{"name":"Epupa Falls","place":"Epupa Falls, Namibia","at":[-16.999,13.246],"text":"Palms and waterfalls on the Kunene, Angola across the river.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Epupa_Falls_%28detail%29.jpg/500px-Epupa_Falls_%28detail%29.jpg","page":"Epupa Falls","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Epupa_Falls_%28detail%29.jpg","credit":"Hans Hillewaert","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Okangwati","place":"Okangwati, Namibia","at":[-17.416,13.272],"text":"Himba villages."},{"name":"Van Zyl's Pass","place":"Van Zyl's Pass, Namibia","at":[-17.633,12.735],"text":"The steep rocky descent, east to west only."},{"name":"Marienfluss","place":"Marienfluss, Namibia","at":[-17.3,12.47],"text":"Grass, fairy circles and silence down to the Kunene.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/MapBantoustanKaokoland.PNG/500px-MapBantoustanKaokoland.PNG","page":"Kaokoland","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MapBantoustanKaokoland.PNG","credit":"Rémih","license":"Public domain"}}],"leg